<title>RUSSIA: Russia seen returning to 15-pct tax on T-bills.</title>
<headline>Russia seen returning to 15-pct tax on T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian Treasury bill and government bond income will be subject to a 15-percent tax rate if new instructions on the application of profits tax law are approved, a senior Finance Ministry offiical said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;In the instructions on tax privileges, new GKO discount treasury bills and those in secondary market trade are taxed at 15 percent,&quot; said Bella Zlatkis, head of the ministry's securities and financial markets department.</p>
<p>She said the draft had been prepared by the Finance Ministry and the State Tax Service, but it still had to be approved by the Ministry of Justice.</p>
</text>
